Subject: [PATCH 1/2] test(issue-87): D1 CA4i progress-stall bound, D2 SC7
 window from the terminal, D3 SC10 per-Task bootstrap release

CA4i: the owner-wide Git gate prepares the 128 claims one at a time with no
total deadline by design, so setup fails only when neither the claim count nor
the S1 count advances for 30 s, instead of a fixed 120 s total.

SC7: the 8 s settlement-poll window starts when the non-success terminal has
been committed and the owner revoked, not when the start task finishes.

SC10: each peer's bootstrap is released at its own Task's Bound instead of
after the last Task's, so another Task's bind latency no longer counts against
the 30 s native bootstrap deadline. Completions are still released together.

No production code, timeout or ownership semantics change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WkCYCfQN5ESKshajCzXndN
